 Walk, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359111"} "High Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359130"} "Pole Vault, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031064"} "Long Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031078"} "Triple Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359198"} "Shot Put, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359221"} "Discus Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359244"} "Hammer Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "359267"} "Javelin Throw, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "63214"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "63901"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "64577"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "65264"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "65963"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "66679"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "257822"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "302147"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000897"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014066"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/120"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Heptathlon, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "12 – 13 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/909"} "Estádio Olímpico João Havelange, Engenho de Dentro, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/359290"} "31 from 21 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Scoring by 1985 point tables."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/124069"} "Jessica Ennis-Hill"] " was the defending gold medallist and had won the 2015 World Championships after coming back from a maternity hiatus. She was expected to be challenged by her countrywoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/126308"} "Katarina Johnson-Thompson"] " and Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/122705"} "Brianne Theisen-Eaton"] ", the 2016 World Indoor Champion in the pentathlon, in the battle of hyphenated names. Theisen-Eaton’s story was intriguing as her husband, American " [:a {:href "/athletes/126672"} "Ashton Eaton"] ", was the heavy favorite in the decathlon. A victory for both would make them the first ever husband-wife to win individual gold medals at the same Olympics, but for different nations."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Ennis-Hill took the early lead by winning the 100 hurdles, her best event. Johnson-Thompson then took over the lead by winning the high jump, clearing 1.98, a new heptathlon world best. Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/129137"} "Nafissatou Thiam"] ", bronze medallist at the 2014 European Championships, won the shot put to take the lead. In the final event of the first day, Johnson-Thompson led the 200 with 23.26, followed by Ennis-Hill in 23.49. After day one, Ennis-Hill led with Thiam in second, Barbadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/129126"} "Akela Jones"] " third, KJT in fourth, and Theisen-Eaton in sixth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Opening the second day, Thiam PRed in the long jump with 6.58 to take a 5-point lead over Ennis-Hill. Thiam PRed again in the javelin with 53.13 to extend her lead, while Ennis-Hill stayed in second, but Theisen-Eaton moved into third place. Ennis-Hill was a superior runner and it was thought she might run down Thiam in the 800, but the Belgian PRed again with 2:16.64, and Jessica’s 2:09.07 was not quite good enough, Thiam winning a surprise gold medal by 35 points. Theisen-Eaton held on for bronze, while Johnson-Thompson struggled on the second day and dropped back to sixth. In keeping with the hyphenated motif, Latvian " [:a {:href "/athletes/123689"} "Laura Ikauniece-Admidina"] " finished fourth. Thiam’s gold medal was the result of her recording five PRs in the seven events."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "380"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129137"} "Nafi Thiam"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} "6810"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "702"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/124069"} "Jessica Ennis-Hill"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "6775"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "497"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122705"} "Brianne Theisen-Eaton"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "6653"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "972"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123689"} "Laura Ikauniece-Admidiņa"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/LAT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/LAT.png"}] "LAT"]] [:td {} "6617"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "777"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130304"} "Carolin Schäfer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-c